WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.072
Everyone trembled in fear.

2
00:00:06.073 --> 00:00:10.466
The captain of the Sleeping Dragon circled the room.

3
00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.815
He was breathing heavily.

4
00:00:12.816 --> 00:00:16.012
"Where is my good-luck bear charm?"

5
00:00:16.013 --> 00:00:19.869
He stopped in front of the boys.

6
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:25.055
"Sir, I swear, I don’t know," Gunnar pleaded.

7
00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:31.281
"Silence! My father gave that bear charm to me when I killed my first bear.

8
00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:34.806
Its power has made me the best bear hunter!

9
00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:37.469
It’s my most precious treasure."

10
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.562
The captain poked Gunnar hard.

11
00:00:40.563 --> 00:00:44.611
Gunnar grabbed Vinnie and said in angry voice,

12
00:00:44.612 --> 00:00:46.857
"Vinnie! Did you take it?

13
00:00:46.858 --> 00:00:48.620
I trusted you!"

14
00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:52.876
"No, no, I didn’t take it," cried Vinnie.

15
00:00:52.877 --> 00:00:56.471
Skull-Crusher looked around the room and roared,

16
00:00:56.472 --> 00:00:58.820
"Where is the girl?"

17
00:00:58.821 --> 00:01:04.804
At that moment, Mandy and Birgitta were returning from the neighbor’s house.

18
00:01:04.805 --> 00:01:10.201
They were about to enter Birgitta’s home through a door near the animals.

19
00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:13.749
The girls could hear an angry voice inside.

20
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.079
Mandy stuck her head in the door.

21
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.952
"It’s Skull-Crusher!" she whispered urgently.

22
00:01:21.953 --> 00:01:24.948
"He looks very angry."

23
00:01:24.949 --> 00:01:28.951
"What should we do?" asked Birgitta anxiously.

24
00:01:28.952 --> 00:01:34.342
"The last time he was this mad, he smashed up our house."

25
00:01:34.343 --> 00:01:37.272
Mandy looked at the animals.

26
00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:40.786
She noticed a lit oil lamp by the door.

27
00:01:40.787 --> 00:01:43.077
She had an idea.

28
00:01:43.078 --> 00:01:50.621
"When I say so, let the animals loose," she instructed Birgitta.

29
00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:52.954
Mandy picked up the lamp.

30
00:01:52.955 --> 00:01:56.877
She placed the flame near one pig’s tail.

31
00:01:56.878 --> 00:02:00.222
"Now!" she cried.

32
00:02:00.223 --> 00:02:06.534
Just as Birgitta opened the pen, the pig felt the heat and rushed forward.

33
00:02:06.535 --> 00:02:12.872
The other animals cried as well and ran through the house.

34
00:02:12.873 --> 00:02:18.033
"Vinnie!" Mandy cried. "Over here!"

35
00:02:18.034 --> 00:02:22.498
Vinnie tried to sneak away, but the captain saw him.

36
00:02:22.499 --> 00:02:28.004
"Stop! Where are you going?" shouted Skull-Crusher.

37
00:02:28.005 --> 00:02:31.484
A fat pig blocked the captain’s way.

38
00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:35.001
Vinnie ran and made it to the back door.

39
00:02:35.002 --> 00:02:39.937
"Mandy, I have to ask you something," he gasped.

40
00:02:39.938 --> 00:02:43.822
Mandy grabbed his hand and started running.

41
00:02:43.823 --> 00:02:45.671
"Ask me later, Vinnie.

42
00:02:45.672 --> 00:02:48.359
Right now, we have to run!"

43
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.934
They kept running until they reached an open field.

44
00:02:52.935 --> 00:02:58.416
It looked like a shipyard.

45
00:02:58.417 --> 00:03:01.805
"Why is the captain so angry?"

46
00:03:01.806 --> 00:03:05.944
Mandy asked, taking a deep breath.

47
00:03:05.945 --> 00:03:10.014
"Somebody took his bear charm," said Vinnie.

48
00:03:10.015 --> 00:03:12.417
"He thinks we did it!"

49
00:03:12.418 --> 00:03:15.879
"His charm? You mean this?"

50
00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.736
Mandy took the little carved bear from her front pocket.

51
00:03:20.737 --> 00:03:24.554
"So you have it!" Vinnie shouted.

52
00:03:24.555 --> 00:03:29.535
"Old Dirk gave it to me!" Mandy cried.

53
00:03:29.536 --> 00:03:33.751
"Well, we have to give it back," said Vinnie.

54
00:03:33.752 --> 00:03:36.420
"And we have to get out of here."

55
00:03:36.421 --> 00:03:40.939
Vinnie pulled the photo out of his pocket and studied it.

56
00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.739
The sail in the photo was still glowing yellow.

57
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:48.480
"It shows a ship with sails," he said.

58
00:03:48.481 --> 00:03:51.405
"But I didn’t see any sails."

59
00:03:51.406 --> 00:03:54.335
Mandy pointed at the photo.

60
00:03:54.336 --> 00:03:58.133
"What are those glowing things on the ship’s side?

61
00:03:58.134 --> 00:04:01.079
They look like big round plates."

62
00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.942
"I don’t know," replied Vinnie.

63
00:04:04.943 --> 00:04:08.016
"But I think we should head back to the harbor."

64
00:04:08.017 --> 00:04:16.991
"And return Skull-Crusher’s charm," said Mandy.

